From 1730fec7519fbe6ffa64fd5236623b51dee084d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrockMr <118761873+CrockMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:48:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose state 0.4 fields and task-row orders in the oracle
 adapter

State schema 0.4 is 0.3 plus characters[].medical, stats, in_something,
carrying, carrying_id and being_carried, health[].bandage, splint and
wear, and squads[].money; 0.1 to 0.3 output is unchanged, order
included (the canonical bytes of all three are pinned on patch 0006 for
a world that holds every 0.4 value). medical reads MedicalState Blood,
Bleeding, Hunger, Fed, Coma and BloodKo, and is null without a medical
state; the part keys read HealthPart Bandage, Rig and Wear. stats holds
the 34 stored stats keyed by the lowercase KenshiLib StatsEnumerated
name, null without a stats object; HIVEMEDIC and VET share Medic's
storage and WEAPONS and SURVIVAL have none, so none of them is a key.
in_something maps Locks.HeldState 0, 1 and 2 to nothing, bed and
prison, anything else to null. carrying is nothing, or character with
the carried character's census id; a carried character outside the
census leaves both null, and Meitou never emits other. money is
Squad.Money, null beyond 1e9 in magnitude. Numbers use the existing
finite, |x| <= 1e9 guard.

In 0.4 order is projected from CharacterCold.Running while it runs the
character's task now, when its row is not 0, not one of the 147
Task_Blank goal rows of docs/game/ai-tasks.md, and has a native name.
The type is looked up by row number in OracleTaskNames, a copy of the
native probe's names in KenshiLib TaskType order (291 rows), never the
Meitou enum's spelling: Meitou's symbols differ at 0, 38, 52, 65, 223,
245, 289 and 290. target_id is the census id of a character target,
position stays null. A goal row reads null, so an attack (row 16) does
not match the original's immediate task; that is documented, not a bug.

dump_state, ping's supported_schema_versions and canonical ordering
accept 0.4, and the default dump schema (ping's schema_version and
state_schema_version) becomes 0.4. The identity-only captures keep 0.2
and discard their output.

The capture stays read-only; tests pin each field and its null cases,
the stats key set and order, the order rule (move and treatment rows,
Task_Blank rows, a stale provenance, row 0, a target outside the
census), the unchanged state hash, 0.4 canonical ordering, and the name
table against the Meitou enum numbering. The shared canonical fixture
is the 69-case copy of KenshiOracle schema/canonical-vectors.json
(four 0.4 cases appended, the 65 earlier cases byte-identical) with its
pin updated.

